## 7. Why Check Before Adding?

Important code:

```
if(set.contains(nums[i])) {
    return true;
}

set.add(nums[i]);
```

We check first because we need to know whether the number appeared earlier.

If it already exists, we return `true`.

Otherwise, we add it.

**Memory trick:**

CHECK → DUPLICATE? → RETURN TRUE\
NOT DUPLICATE → ADD TO SET

