## 9. Important Interview Questions

**Q1. What is HashSet in Java?**

HashSet is a collection that stores unique elements and does not allow duplicates.

**Q2. Does HashSet allow duplicate values?**

No. Duplicate elements are not added.

**Q3. What does `contains()` do?**

It checks whether an element is already present.

**Q4. What does `add()` do?**

It adds an element if it is not already present.

**Q5. Why do we check before adding?**

To detect whether the current number appeared earlier.

**Q6. What is the average time complexity of HashSet `contains()`?**

O(1).

**Q7. What is the space complexity of this solution?**

O(n), because the HashSet can store up to n unique elements.

**Q8. Why return true immediately?**

Because finding even one duplicate is enough to answer the problem.

